# PoCP Capability Internet Protocol

## Definition

PoCP Capability Internet Protocol is a decentralized contribution, invocation, settlement, and reputation protocol for AI capability and compute networks.

It allows distributed Entities to:

- register identity;
- run nodes;
- publish capabilities;
- discover capabilities;
- invoke other nodes;
- submit proofs;
- verify work;
- settle value;
- build reputation;
- participate in governance.

## Core Chain

```text
Entity
→ NodeProfile
→ PublicNodeEndpoint
→ Capability
→ Invocation
→ Proof
→ Verification
→ Settlement
→ TokenAccount
→ ReputationGraph
→ ProtocolEvent
```

## Positioning

PoCP AI Commons is the first reference application.

The larger goal is to become the capability internet protocol for distributed AI and compute networks.

## Principle

Do not build only an AI platform.

Build the protocol that allows AI capabilities to become a network.
